<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="022" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>spaarke_show_decisions and app-only paging tool</title>
    <phase>B MCP host and tools</phase>
    <gate>after 015, 017 and 021</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; new tool classes and tests (.cs, .ts)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive output control: FR-04 keeps privileged legal detail out of model-visible text (ADR-015); a mistake is a confidentiality leak</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds only its own tool files, parity fixture and tests; shares no file with 023, 024 or 030</parallel-reason>
    <deps>015, 017, 021</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, endpoints, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement spaarke_show_decisions (model- and app-visible, readOnly, closed optional category enum) returning a short text summary with Console deep links, page 1 of slim rows and a widget pointer, with privileged Work Items reduced to one neutral count line in everything the model sees; and the app-only readOnly paging tool (working name spaarke_list_decision_page) that returns later pages with full detail.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in MCP tool design, ADR-015 data minimisation and cross-language parity testing.</role>
  <goal>Both tools are listed with correct annotations and visibility; category counts match the Console's laneCountFilters.ts partition through a shared parity fixture; the privileged-marker negative test passes; every result is under 64 KiB at 200 items; the final paging tool name is recorded in notes/decisions.md.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-03, FR-04, FR-05, FR-14, NFR-02, NFR-05; design §7.1 and §9.5. laneCountFilters.ts after #2579: LaneFilterKey = 'all' | 'invoiceDecisions' | 'other' | WorkType; Invoice decisions card right after All, only when non-empty; work-type cards and Other are computed over the non-billing rest. Paging tool choice: notes/decisions.md 2026-11-06.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/ShowDecisionsTool.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/ListDecisionPageTool.cs (final name fixed here per the naming note)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/DecisionsTextSummary.cs (content text, Console deep links, privilege reduction)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/DecideLaneCategories.cs (closed enum + partition mirroring laneCountFilters.ts)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/fixtures/decide-lane-category-parity/cases.json</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Mcp/DecideLaneCategoriesParityTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/__tests__/laneCountFilters.parity.test.ts</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/ShowDecisionsToolTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/PrivilegeReductionTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/laneCountFilters.ts (bucketLaneItems; LaneFilterKey L32; invoiceDecisions L69-71)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/fixtures/compose-citation-parity/cases.json (shared C#/TS parity fixture style)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/WorklistItemSummary.cs and IDecisionCapability.ListDecidePageAsync (from 015)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="015" status="pending">WorklistItemSummary, PrivilegeFlagged and the paged list</dependency>
      <dependency task="017" status="pending">DecisionResultMapper.ToToolError</dependency>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">A10 auth, per-tool policies and the annotation guard</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Every MCP tool added by this task is named spaarke_{verb}_{object} (naming note §1), tagged with area legal-operations, carries an explicit readOnlyHint and a title, and has a description of at most 1,024 characters phrased 'use for / not for'; app-only tools set _meta.ui visibility to app only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">In content and structuredContent of spaarke_show_decisions, every Work Item whose PrivilegeFlagged is true is reduced to the single line 'N privileged items — open to review' with no matter name, reason, evidence or party name; full detail for those items is returned only by the app-only paging tool.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">spaarke_show_decisions' input schema has exactly one optional property, category, a closed enum of the Decide lane's LaneFilterKey values (all, invoiceDecisions, other and the Decide-lane work types in laneCountFilters.ts), with additionalProperties false; the paging tool's input is the cursor only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Category counts are computed by DecideLaneCategories, which mirrors bucketLaneItems; a shared fixture tests/fixtures/decide-lane-category-parity/cases.json is asserted by both an xunit and a jest test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">structuredContent of spaarke_show_decisions carries page 1 (at most 50 summaries), the next cursor, the per-category counts and consoleBaseUrl (the Console URL the widget uses for link-outs); _meta.ui points at ui://spaarke/decisions.html.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every tool this task adds reads the request HttpContext from IHttpContextAccessor and passes it (or its User) to the decision capability. A null HttpContext or an unauthenticated caller returns an isError result with UserContextRequired (DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED) before any capability call, and nothing falls back to an app-only client (FR-10 as amended 2026-11-07, option C; ADR-002 WP-6 fail closed). No ICallerContext or other caller holder is introduced.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Every domain failure from a tool added by this task is returned as an isError tool result produced by DecisionResultMapper.ToToolError → Api/Mcp/McpToolResults (reasonCode plus a fix-the-call message); no domain failure is returned as a transport error or exception.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every result of a tool added by this task is under 64 KiB at 200 seeded Work Items (NFR-02).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Tools added by this task inject only the decision capability, IDecisionLookupSearch and Api/Mcp helpers: no AI-internal type (Services/Ai/**, IChatClient, playbook services).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">File ownership for parallel safety: this task adds only its own files under Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/ and its own test files; tools are discovered per area by attribute (set up in 020), so no shared registration file is edited.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Every log statement or telemetry property this task adds records identifiers, sizes, timings and outcome/reason codes only: no bearer token, claim value, record text or tool argument (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

