  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read laneCountFilters.ts and write the parity fixture (cases of mixed billing, matter and work-type items with expected cards and counts); make the jest parity test pass against bucketLaneItems.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement DecideLaneCategories in C# and make the xunit parity test pass on the same fixture.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement DecisionsTextSummary: counts per category, the top 5 non-privileged items each with a Console deep link built from the existing Console URL settings, and the privileged count line.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement ShowDecisionsTool (capability ListDecidePageAsync(httpContext.User, null) with the HttpContext from IHttpContextAccessor → summary text, structuredContent page 1 with privileged rows reduced, _meta.ui) and the paging tool (app-only, cursor → full summaries); fix the paging tool's final name per the naming note and record it in notes/decisions.md.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the contract, privilege and size tests (seed 200 items across at least 3 matters, including privileged items with a unique marker string in reason and matter name).</step>
    <step order="6">Run the suites; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If no existing setting or builder gives the Console URL for a Work Item deep link, STOP and escalate rather than hard-coding a URL.</trigger>
    <trigger>If laneCountFilters.ts' partition cannot be mirrored exactly (e.g. depends on client-only state), STOP and escalate with the case.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any privileged detail would have to appear in model-visible output to satisfy another criterion, STOP: FR-04 wins; escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>REST GET /api/v1/signals/worklist (SignalReadEndpoints.cs) and the client partition laneCountFilters.ts; no MCP tool exists in the BFF.</existing>
    <extension>They are the extension: thin adapters over IDecisionCapability; the only new logic is the category partition (mirrored, parity-tested) and the privilege reduction FR-04 requires.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Copilot cannot list a user's Work Items (FR-03), the widget cannot page past 50 items (FR-05), and without the reduction privileged detail would reach the model (FR-04).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Install (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund), build and test TypeScript projects</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/ShowDecisionsTool.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/ListDecisionPageTool.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/DecisionsTextSummary.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/DecideLaneCategories.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/PrivilegeReductionTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/ShowDecisionsToolTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/fixtures/decide-lane-category-parity/cases.json</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">tools/list includes spaarke_show_decisions (visible to model and app, readOnlyHint true, title, description of at most 1,024 characters with 'use for / not for') and the paging tool (app-only visibility, readOnlyHint true).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">spaarke_show_decisions' input schema has only the optional closed category enum and additionalProperties false.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">For the seeded user, the per-category counts equal the Console's Decide-lane partition: the parity fixture passes in both the xunit and the jest test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an invalid category value returns an isError result whose message lists the valid values (not a transport error).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (FR-04): with a privileged Work Item seeded with a unique marker string in its reason and matter name, the marker appears in neither content nor structuredContent of spaarke_show_decisions, and the 'N privileged items — open to review' count is correct; the paging tool's result for that page does carry the item's detail.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With 200 seeded items: every result of both tools is under 64 KiB; paging returns each item exactly once in Console order; a stale cursor returns the remaining items without duplicates; a malformed cursor returns isError ontology.worklist.cursor_invalid.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">FR-14: content alone (widget ignored) lists counts per category and the top items with Console deep links; no write tool is model-visible.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the worklist's 503 too_many_signals becomes an isError result with that reasonCode, not a transport error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A log-capture test shows per-call telemetry has tool name, latency, row count, outcome and correlation id, and no argument or record text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The final paging tool name is recorded in notes/decisions.md; the PR records the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Request one seeding proof for the privileged-marker test (confidentiality guard): stop reducing one privileged row, confirm the test fails, restore. The jest parity test lives beside the existing laneCountFilters tests and must not change laneCountFilters.ts.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
